\newlabel{fig:noisegates}{{3}{7}{Five candidate noise gates against the one recording identified by ear as noise. Four place it mid-distribution or in the wrong tail, so catching it costs 43 to 89\,\% of the corpus. The only statistic on which it is extreme is the share of energy below 400\,Hz, which was a segmentation defect, not a gate.\relax }{figure.caption.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The synthesis chain. Two gesture contours drive the oscillator; turbulence, the $f_0$-tracking resonance and the fixed tracheal comb shape the result. The dashed blocks are implemented, parity-tested and off by default: their published physics is not in doubt, but their hand-set default parameter sets lost their pre-registered bake-offs, and only the per-species fits ship, per type, where they win.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:signalchain}{{4}{7}{The synthesis chain. Two gesture contours drive the oscillator; turbulence, the $f_0$-tracking resonance and the fixed tracheal comb shape the result. The dashed blocks are implemented, parity-tested and off by default: their published physics is not in doubt, but their hand-set default parameter sets lost their pre-registered bake-offs, and only the per-species fits ship, per type, where they win.\relax }{figure.caption.6}{}}
