\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces The fitted gestures behind the three acoustic examples. Every syllable in the corpus is two named physical contours (air-sac pressure and labial tension), not a latent code, and this is the whole of the interpretability claim. The dashed line is the tension clamp of the parameterisation; a contour that rides it is at a limit of the parameterisation and not at a fitted value, which happens in 6\,617 of 12\,724 types across the production learn.\relax }}{14}{figure.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gestures}{{8}{14}{The fitted gestures behind the three acoustic examples. Every syllable in the corpus is two named physical contours (air-sac pressure and labial tension), not a latent code, and this is the whole of the interpretability claim. The dashed line is the tension clamp of the parameterisation; a contour that rides it is at a limit of the parameterisation and not at a fitted value, which happens in 6\,617 of 12\,724 types across the production learn.\relax }{figure.caption.10}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{Two of those four adoptions have now been re-judged on the bench. They disagree.}{14}{section*.14}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{The two-voice adoption was re-judged next, on twelve times the population, and it held.}{14}{section*.15}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces What the physical model reproduces, and what it misses. Three fitted types, taken from the top, the middle and the bottom of the resynthesis-cosine ordering over the types whose members have cached audio; the corpus median is 0.699 over 16\,239 types, so the middle row is a median type, not a chosen success. Top: a clean descending whistle, which the oscillator and its tracking tract reproduce closely. Middle: the median case. The pitch is right, and the pulse train that carries the real syllable's timbre is replaced by a steady tone. Bottom: a failure, and the third panel says why. The type's member contours disagree by kilohertz, so the cluster median the fit starts from describes no member well. The cosine is the objective the fit optimised and ranks audible fidelity \emph  {inversely} (Section~\ref  {sec:walls}).\relax }}{15}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:spectral}{{9}{15}{What the physical model reproduces, and what it misses. Three fitted types, taken from the top, the middle and the bottom of the resynthesis-cosine ordering over the types whose members have cached audio; the corpus median is 0.699 over 16\,239 types, so the middle row is a median type, not a chosen success. Top: a clean descending whistle, which the oscillator and its tracking tract reproduce closely. Middle: the median case. The pitch is right, and the pulse train that carries the real syllable's timbre is replaced by a steady tone. Bottom: a failure, and the third panel says why. The type's member contours disagree by kilohertz, so the cluster median the fit starts from describes no member well. The cosine is the objective the fit optimised and ranks audible fidelity \emph {inversely} (Section~\ref {sec:walls}).\relax }{figure.caption.11}{}}
